    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Import purchase order items</title>

  <p>Some vendors send their invoice as a spreadsheet. <gui>Load items from
  file</gui> in <link xref="unprocessed_po"/> reads it onto the purchase
  order, instead of typing each quantity and price.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>File</gui>: a .csv or .xls file whose first row
    holds the column names. Its rows are shown on the right.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose which of its columns is the <gui>Qty</gui>, the
    <gui>Order number</gui> and the <gui>Price</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Import to PO</gui>. The order's lines on the left take
    the file's quantities and prices, and each order number is matched to the
    product with that vendor order number.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check the lines, then click <gui>Save PO items</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <note><p>The file's rows are matched to the order's lines by position: the
  first row goes to line 1, the second to line 2, and so on. The file must
  list the products in the same order as the purchase order, with no more
  rows than it has lines.</p></note>

  <p><gui>Reload PO</gui> shows the order's lines as they are saved, undoing
  an import that was not saved.</p>

</page>
